<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mawokota</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mawokota is one of the original core counties of the Kingdom of Buganda, south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kampala">Kampala</a>, today in Mpigi District of Uganda, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-victoria">Lake Victoria</a>. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/busiro">Busiro</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyadondo">Kyadondo</a> it formed the area where, according to historians, a group of clans first accepted a common ruler, the kabaka, around the fourteenth or fifteenth century.</p></div>
